  killsNeededToUnlockDesc: 1
  shortStory: "Under the low full moon, Maya heard the heavy flapping of wings. Above,
    the severed upper torso of a woman glided through the night, her long, tubular
    tongue uncoiling as she hunted.\r\n\r\nWaiting for the creature to fly toward
    the fields, Maya slipped behind an abandoned hut. Hidden in the weeds sat the
    lower half of the creature\u2019s body\u2014standing rigid and lifeless.\r\n\r\nMaya
    pulled out a jar of sea salt and garlic, pouring it over the raw, exposed waist
    of the lower torso.\r\n\r\nA blood-curdling shriek pierced the night as the returning
    upper half thrashed desperately to reconnect. But the salt burned like fire.
    Trapped in agony, the creature writhed helplessly as the first light of dawn
    broke\u2014turning her to ash before she could ever complete herself again.\r\n"
